WEBVTT

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:08.120
We all believed that there was only one continuum.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.830
That time and history is the same for all of us.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:14.440
Time never repeats itself.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.750
We'd never have considered the possibility

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.370
that some might be living out a different history from our own.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:01.790
Hey, Megu-chan, you're soft for those who come to depend on you.

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:03.210
The maternal type, right?

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.210
What? What's that about?

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.400
Shiratori-san, why don't you sit down?

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.860
Oh, how could I?!

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.510
It's priority that women come first.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:14.080
Don't be so rigid! Come sit!

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:17.420
Please! It's not proper for a woman to come in contact with a man so causally!

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.480
You're adorable!

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:20.630
Please, you must cease this!

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:21.700
Minato-san!

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.410
Why don't the three of us sit comfortably together?

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.830
Please, you mustn't!

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:27.340
Minato-san!

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.360
Wow!

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:34.920
The Beginning of "Nadesico's War"

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:37.130
Look at it bob about like that.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:39.210
I bet those two are fighting back inside.

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:40.730
Can't we establish a comm link?

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:41.340
All right!

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.930
Hey, answer me! I said answer me, damn it!

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.120
How bizarre! A vulgar man's face has appeared in midair!

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:50.110
Well, that's a...

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:50.860
Mark my words, you jerk!

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:54.150
After I'm done rescuing those two, I'll thrash you into pieces, bastard!

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.070
Easy...

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.580
Megumi-chan, we'll be right over soon, so...

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.010
What was that?

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:00.860
The enemy, the enemy.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:03.330
From here on out, it's Jovian territory.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:04.660
Guess we're in bit of a bind.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.290
But we can't just abandon them!

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:08.080
All right!

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.040
Here we go!

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:15.840
You were saying?

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:16.840
Shut up!

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:21.680
Say, I was thinking. Does that person look somewhat familiar?

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.920
He said he liked Gekiganger.

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:29.790
Yeah, he's got the same aura that Yamada Jiro-san gave off.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:30.890
You...

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.570
I thought so too.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:37.970
Pretending that he was dead, but then reappearing as a rival after signing up with the enemy.

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:40.160
Sounds like a plot twist he'd be really into.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.630
I can't see, you bastards!

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:44.700
The bullet was stopped by a silver dollar, perhaps?

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:47.120
The Bible and metal lighters are also valid scenarios for this.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.390
Enough of that!

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:50.640
Gai would never do something like that.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:54.540
Yeah, he liked Gekiganger and he liked to be a real showoff,

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.630
but he wouldn't get innocent people involved.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:00.320
So, we've been fighting people all this time?

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:06.360
It appears that life-forms are no longer barred from going though the Chulips.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.770
From lizards to humans...

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.250
Confirming signal!

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:18.270
Following descent, landing at the Nergal underground docking bay.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:20.490
Wow, that was fast!

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:22.010
Landing in progress.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:24.070
It couldn't be Gai.

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:38.710
So, this is the Shakuyaku?

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:41.850
The enemy seem to have gotten wind of our intentions.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:43.310
Clearly they're focusing their targets

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:47.130
on our phase transition engine and boson jumping research facilities.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.890
Well, let's see.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:53.510
If they were human beings, they would surmise as much.

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:55.140
This is no time to sulk!

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:57.900
Our current worry is to launch the Shakuyaku successfully.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.840
The Third Reclamation of Mars...

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:05.980
Since cooperation between the military and Nergal has yielded dramatic results,

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:09.330
the chairman wishes that our original objectives be put back into focus.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:13.850
In any case, boson jump experimentation requires massive amounts of CCs,

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:15.530
which only can be found on Mars.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:17.360
The company, the company, the company!

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.060
Of course, I'm not one to talk like that.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.160
All of humanity is hoping for the successful retaking of Mars!

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:26.140
It's proof enough that even a goofy crew like them

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:28.790
went this far for the sake of Mars!

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:34.710
But will they follow our lead even after they've learned the truth?

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:38.570
The Shakuyaku will be launched in total secrecy with a handpicked crew on board.

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:41.460
The Nadesico will act as a decoy to draw the enemy's attention.

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:43.670
The operation will begin in twelve hours.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:48.260
Please, Won-san, do something with him!

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:50.290
He won't let me go unless he can talk to you.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:54.670
Hey, what sort of evil scheme are you brewing up this time?

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:58.540
I sure would love to hear about it too, you know? What do you say?!

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:01.380
Admiral, please!

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:06.950
Fine, I'll let you in on our evil scheme.

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:11.130
All right, lock in the pit, and close the breast plate panel!

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.670
So all the basics are the same, except it's a lot bigger!

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:24.110
Bigger means it takes more time, so get yourselves together!

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:25.110
Right!

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.840
Once you figure it out, it isn't that special.

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.190
Think we'll handle them all right once we figure out their pattern?

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:35.370
A broken textile machine?

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:36.620
One pattern.

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:39.330
What's going on?! They knew about all this?!

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:43.900
Both Nergal and the military knew we were fighting people?

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:45.380
But why?!

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:49.330
Why do you know something that I didn't even know?!

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:52.380
Why you little...

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:54.180
I don't know, Admiral.

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:57.450
People may not take well to you dragging a female officer to your quarters.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.420
Pilots don't have anything to do with this!

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:01.100
My, my, aren't we shameless.

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:03.070
Shameless?!

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:04.640
This person is actually...

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:08.560
You're...

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.130
Yes, I'm afraid so.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.700
Ban
Intruding into Private Lines is Forbidden

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:14.120
Oh, my!

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:19.040
Modern protection mechanisms are such a pain for this old man.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:22.480
There is a way to bypass the privacy lockout.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:24.960
I say, modern girls are really something!

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:28.350
We can't have a secret on this ship, can we?

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:31.350
Dirty, aren't you?

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:42.120
You certainly are something!

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.780
What are you doing, Ruri-chan?

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:46.530
All done.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:50.750
I'll get right to the point.

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:55.760
The Jovian Lizards are actually those who were banished one hundred years ago.

00:07:56.890 --> 00:07:57.870
Banished?

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:00.210
Earthlings.

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.570
Gekigan Net!

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:04.710
Gantan...

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:09.160
It's hopeless! It's too flexible.

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:12.030
Stretching out and shrinking back, it's like it was made of Moji.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:13.970
Moji? That's it, Moji!

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:15.060
What is it, Joe?

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:18.890
Remember how Junpei-kun and Nanako-san were eating Moji?

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:21.990
Moji are soft while hot,

00:08:23.010 --> 00:08:24.730
but they harden when cooled!

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:27.400
I got it, Joe! If we can only cool off that sucker!

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:29.600
He'll be a cinch to beat!

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:31.320
All right, leave it to me!

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:33.800
Let's Gekiga-In!

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:35.240
Riku Gangar!

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:38.160
How are you doing, Ladies?

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:42.430
If you have any requests, please feel free to make yourself heard.

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:43.080
Oh, no.

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:45.910
But I thought we were prisoners.

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:48.000
But you are women before you are prisoners.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.500
Thou shalt treasure women!

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:52.840
I see.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:55.260
Note: Yuujin = Superior Human
Jupiter Yuujin's Battle Ship - Yumemizuki

00:08:57.490 --> 00:08:59.720
We are not like the barbaric, ignorant masses of the Earth.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.180
The youth of the Jovian Federation

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:05.380
are taught to conduct themselves properly when around women.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:06.940
Here I go!

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:09.330
Watch me, Mom! Musashino Hell Tour Attack!

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:11.640
You really love Gekiganger.

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:13.310
Well, yes, it's our bible.

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:18.060
Say, you're the captain of this ship, but why did you go into battle yourself?

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:19.880
Riding that robot?

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:22.130
What, the Tettsujin?

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:28.380
Only a righteous warrior adept at many things is entrusted with command.

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:31.350
Which means we must also be ready as ace pilots.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:37.770
That's just a loyal pet.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:39.940
Please, come this way.

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:44.440
As you can see, they also double as computational units inside the ship.

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:47.650
We are short on manpower.

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:51.120
So only a small number of people can go through the Chulip.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:51.400
Yes.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:52.330
Yuujin

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:56.110
We're the glorious culmination that came about through organic leap experimentation!
Yuujin

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:57.910
The Yuujin Forces!

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:00.430
Megumi-chan, are you all right?

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:01.130
Yes...

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:04.010
How inconsiderate of me! I will have a medic rush to your side at once!

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:04.790
Oh, I'm fine.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:08.800
Guess there really are Jovian Lizards.

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:11.840
How could such people as you commit such horrendous...

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:13.920
Far more horrendous acts were committed by your people!

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:18.790
Genichirou, you're all right?

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.310
Well, it was getting a little hairy

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:24.310
when I suddenly found myself transported to the Moon of two weeks ago.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:28.960
But you're the ones who dropped Chulips onto Mars first.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:30.640
Chulips?

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:32.320
They're talking about the dimensional leap gates.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:36.610
Then say so! Don't use such strange words, you simpleton!

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:39.170
You're the one around here who's strange.

00:10:39.590 --> 00:10:42.680
The reason we moved into Mars two years ago,

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:45.370
was because you were after Jupiter.

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:47.210
We were?

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:01.500
A certain incident that's been wiped clean from our history textbooks

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:03.220
happened one hundred years ago.

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:07.870
After getting burned by the independence movement

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:09.640
that sprung up in the autonomous districts of the Moon,

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.500
the UE infiltrated the movement,

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:15.460
orchestrating a breakup into two camps, the separatists and the moderates,

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:18.280
then manipulating a vicious purge between the two.

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:23.190
I know about the War of the Lunar Autonomous Districts!

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:29.090
Couldn't it be that they just taught you what to know?

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:32.090
In fact, the Federation was deeply involved in the civil war,

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:36.510
finally forcefully banishing those who refused to accept a Federation presence.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:42.560
So they disappeared to Mars, the asteroid belt, and Jupiter.

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:43.540
The End.

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:48.100
The UE Government eliminated all records of their existence.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.280
They never even existed.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.800
Why did they have to erase all records about them?

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:57.290
The UE probably wanted to cover up their covert operations.

00:11:58.890 --> 00:12:00.970
But I think there were other reasons as well.

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:04.980
Dirty Earthlings justified their robbery of the Moon from us under the guise

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:06.290
of the pacification of an unstable Moon.

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:10.450
We headed to Mars,
where colonization had already begun!

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:14.120
But then the UE fired nuclear warheads at us!

00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:17.710
We were forced off Mars as well!

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:23.440
It was all part of a cover-up. All to keep Earth prosperous and safe.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:27.580
Only Jupiter and its satellites were left for us.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:30.610
That was where we found it.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:31.480
It?

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:43.250
A factory plant?

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:46.190
You could say it's a phase transition engine factory.

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:48.130
The phase transition engine,

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:51.800
unmanned weapons such as the Battas and Jiros, the Chulips...

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:57.410
When they found those plants on Jupiter, they built their own nation-state.

00:12:57.890 --> 00:12:59.870
That's why they are attacking us.

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:01.220
For revenge.

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:04.500
I can't disclose something like this.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:05.930
There is no need to disclose it.

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:07.230
Yes, there is!

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:09.520
You were listening in?!

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:11.060
And you're a captain?

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:12.170
I am a captain!

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:14.160
That's why I have a right to know!

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:17.440
To know who we are fighting.

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:20.870
Nothing will change now that you do know! We're at war!

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:25.330
Those who are on the front lines, those who might lose their lives,

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:27.230
I cannot tell them, "you don't need to know!"

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:40.130
Starting excavation for the Infinity Cannon!

00:13:44.570 --> 00:13:46.770
Beginning the fabrication of mass projectiles.

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:48.870
Extend Infinity Cannon!

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:52.980
Daimajin ready for operations.

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:54.960
Break a leg, Genichirou.

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:57.570
Right, I'll destroy their contortion buffer from the inside.

00:13:59.470 --> 00:14:00.430
Please wait!

00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:02.570
Inside is the Nadesico...

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:04.630
How utterly shameless I've been, but...

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:06.200
Forgive us, but we must...

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:07.710
Excuse me.

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:08.930
Here you are!

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:11.050
You could have thrown those away.

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:12.610
Oh, we wouldn't dare.

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:15.460
Have you completed duplication of the long-lost episode?

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:18.550
Yes, and the condition was superb!

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:19.090
What?!

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:23.320
Tsukumo, are you talking about the legendary episode 13?

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:26.480
Not only that, but the great episodes 9 and 33 as well.

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:28.570
What? Are you serious?!

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:30.430
Too freaking cool!

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:36.020
No matter how powerful our foe may be,

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:38.310
the Yuujin Force is the last vanguard!

00:14:38.610 --> 00:14:40.730
Our fist of steel shall strike and shatter our enemy!

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:42.150
Daimajin,

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:43.070
Go!

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:47.580
The green Earth!

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:48.950
The blue Earth!

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:50.530
We will protect it!

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:53.530
Gekigan Punch!

00:14:56.730 --> 00:14:59.130
Strength of the distortion field around the colony has decreased.

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:00.250
Hostiles?

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:02.110
Raise field to full power!

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:03.340
What about the Shakuyaku?

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:04.550
It doesn't look promising.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:07.650
They're still in the process of attaching the last module.

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:08.890
Fire!

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:17.230
The Shakuyaku!

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:19.620
My heart sinks...

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:22.590
If only the Earthlings appreciated love and life as we do.

00:15:26.600 --> 00:15:27.230
What?!

00:15:28.590 --> 00:15:29.410
Got him.

00:15:29.410 --> 00:15:32.210
Anti-ship missiles can't be replaced easily.
Make them count!

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:32.940
I understand!

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:39.500
You're no threat with your pattern cracked!

00:15:40.050 --> 00:15:41.920
All right. Now hurry it up!

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:43.900
There's no reason why something

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:46.090
that's meant for the fourth vessel can't fit the first vessel.

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:47.220
Yes, Boss!

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:50.480
But are you sure about this?

00:15:50.830 --> 00:15:53.270
Nadesico and Shakuyaku have a very different electrical setup.

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:54.800
At worst, we might explode.

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:56.180
It's okay, it's okay!

00:15:56.650 --> 00:15:57.730
I believe in you!

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:02.770
We'll work something out. Wait three minutes!

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:05.820
Are you sure we can attach the Y Unit?

00:16:06.220 --> 00:16:08.850
The Nadesico's power grid is set up differently from the Shakuyaku.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:14.480
Nevertheless, the Shakuyaku has been crushed, and it's such a waste.

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:14.940
A was...

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:18.460
You're suppose to eat every last grain of rice at a meal.

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:22.640
Ruri-chan, please have the factory people evacuated to the Nadesico.

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:23.040
Aye.

00:16:23.530 --> 00:16:27.410
Damn it, we'd be able to take off if we could only use the catapult.

00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:31.360
But Akito-kun's fighting another person, right?

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:38.060
Justice will always prevail!

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:41.860
Shut up already, damn it!

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:42.620
Wait!

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:44.230
Listen to what we have to say!

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:45.570
You dirty rotten Jovians!

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:48.630
You're mistaken, Akito-san. Please stop attacking!

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:52.690
I want to make this clear so this man's honor is not questioned.

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:54.660
We are not hostages.

00:16:54.940 --> 00:16:58.350
We've all been tricked! These people are...

00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:00.730
Human beings, descendents of those expelled from the Moon.

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:02.670
Please move out of the way!

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:06.710
Our only target is the phase transition power plant- equipped battleship.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:08.990
Shut up! I will protect the Nadesico!

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:10.990
Why are you stuck fighting such an old war?

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:12.260
You don't understand!

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:14.460
This has become our war now!

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:16.130
Get out of that robot now!

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:17.170
Akito!

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:27.650
I've been trapped inside?!

00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:32.070
That's the Nadesico?

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:37.900
Enemy robot is trapped within the field.

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:41.350
Two against one isn't a fair fight. This makes it even.

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:44.320
No, it doesn't. The enemy can boson jump.

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:45.370
No, he won't.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:46.780
How can you say something like that?

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:50.020
Because Megu-chan and Minato-san are on board that robot.

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:53.930
Yes, normal people can't withstand the stresses of boson jumping.

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:58.280
He'll jump. He'll sacrifice those two. He's our enemy!

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:02.520
This is the only way I know how to fight.

00:18:02.730 --> 00:18:04.440
Organic leap now, Tsukumo!

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.470
I can't do that.

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:11.930
How dastardly! Just what do you think a fight between men...

00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:12.490
Well, I'm a woman!

00:18:13.870 --> 00:18:14.270
What's wrong?!

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:19.590
This is for all the people you killed on Mars!

00:18:19.590 --> 00:18:20.890
Stop! Akito-san.

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:21.100
Please stop this!

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:22.420
Not yet! Not yet!

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:23.050
Wait!

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:27.030
The Daimajin no longer has the capacity to engage in combat.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:28.460
I'll let these two out!

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:31.130
After that, fight me one on one!

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:33.920
Stop! Please stop this!

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:36.500
What's the sense in doing something like this,

00:18:36.890 --> 00:18:37.910
Akito-san?!

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:39.800
I'm doing to this to protect the Earth!

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:42.080
Are those who protect the Earth,

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:44.220
those who fight in the war better than regular people?

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:46.060
This is wrong!

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:48.720
This isn't at all like you, Akito-san!

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:51.560
Why can't we get by without fighting a war?!

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:54.940
What's wrong with staying at home and watching Gekiganger?!

00:18:55.430 --> 00:18:57.280
That's so much more like you, Akito-san!

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:01.200
More like you... Be more like you, Akito-san.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:08.480
Yeah, that would be more like me.

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:09.390
But...

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:12.130
That's not who I wanted to be.

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:16.030
You see, I was not a grownup watching Gekiganger,

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:17.910
but a kid who thought I could become Gekiganger.

00:19:18.530 --> 00:19:20.970
UEAF descending from lunar orbit.

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:24.930
Feels like they were watching to see the outcome first.

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:27.750
It was only blind luck that saved us, Captain.

00:19:28.190 --> 00:19:30.530
Just tell me, what do you actually believe in?

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:33.720
Go.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:35.310
Thank you.

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:38.400
Could you tell me your name? My name is...

00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:41.410
I don't want to learn the name of the man I'm trying to kill.

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:43.080
I see. Farewell.

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:51.760
I did what I had to do.

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:53.500
It's all right.

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:57.020
Before, when you rescued both the Captain and me,

00:19:57.610 --> 00:20:01.830
you were more worried about the Captain than me.

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:06.010
But you couldn't forgive yourself for thinking like that,

00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:08.190
so you said "Then, Yurika!"

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:11.350
You're reading in too much.

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:15.610
If you weren't that kind of a person, then I wouldn't have fallen for you.

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:16.880
But...

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:18.500
I'm sorry!

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:19.570
Megumi-chan!

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:23.910
Let it go, let it go. Let it all go!

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:27.390
What the hell are you talking about?!

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:28.880
What? What?

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:32.210
Permission has been granted for the transfer of the evacuated personnel.

00:20:33.510 --> 00:20:35.520
Changing heading to specified colony.

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:39.880
BAKA-bakka.

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:46.970
Hello, Munetake-chan here!

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:49.460
My head is about to explode with everything happening.

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:51.530
It's all because the military top brass is blaming me

00:21:51.530 --> 00:21:54.210
for the Nadesico crew finding out the secret of the Jovian Lizards.

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:57.210
I may look like this, but I really throw myself into my job, so this is a shock!

00:21:57.310 --> 00:21:59.440
In a time like this, what I need is a new robot!

00:21:59.440 --> 00:22:01.730
What? How about making 1 / 48th scale dioramas?

00:22:01.730 --> 00:22:03.210
I have no time for that! Jeez!

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:04.930
Next Martian Successor Nadesico:

00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:07.300
"It Was a Reunion That Came Too Late".
Let's watch it, everyone!

00:22:07.750 --> 00:22:09.720
Will you able to survive?

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:11.450
I'm seriously worried!
